IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `roc-core`
IMPORT `roc-definitions`

-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 9, RULES 10 TO 19: parties, consolidation, security for costs, particulars, pleadings, summary
-- judgment, agreement on facts and law.  Part roc2, layer 1.  How to read a result: see roc2-order-9a.l4 and
-- NOTES.md ("Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (roc2)").  Every answer is subject to O 3 r 2(1) (roc1).

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 9, Rule 10 -- adding and removing of parties`
-- ===========================================================================

DECLARE `o 9 r 10(1) a power of the Court` IS ONE OF
    `o 9 r 10(1) add or remove one or more claimants or defendants`
    `o 9 r 10(1) give permission for a defendant to issue a third party notice in accordance with Order 10`
    `o 9 r 10(1) give directions for the originating process to be served on a person who may have an interest in the action`

-- src:847 | 10. —(1) The Court may add or remove one or more claimants or defendants, give permission for a defendant to issue a third party notice in accordance with Order 10, or give directions for the originating process to be served on any person who may have an interest in the action. (2) Any person seeking to be added as a party may attend a case conference if the person is aware of it or may seek a case conference by letter addressed to the Court and copied to all the parties.
@ref O 9 r 10(1) (src:847)
GIVEN power IS A `o 9 r 10(1) a power of the Court`
      `the person may have an interest in the action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 10(1) the Court may do this` MEANS
    CONSIDER power
    WHEN `o 9 r 10(1) add or remove one or more claimants or defendants` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 9 r 10(1) give permission for a defendant to issue a third party notice in accordance with Order 10` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 9 r 10(1) give directions for the originating process to be served on a person who may have an interest in the action` THEN
        IF `the person may have an interest in the action`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any person who may have an interest in the action"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

DECLARE `o 9 r 10(2) a way a person seeking to be added may proceed` IS ONE OF
    `o 9 r 10(2) attend a case conference`
    `o 9 r 10(2) seek a case conference by letter`

-- src:847 | 10. —(1) The Court may add or remove one or more claimants or defendants, give permission for a defendant to issue a third party notice in accordance with Order 10, or give directions for the originating process to be served on any person who may have an interest in the action. (2) Any person seeking to be added as a party may attend a case conference if the person is aware of it or may seek a case conference by letter addressed to the Court and copied to all the parties.
@ref O 9 r 10(2) (src:847)
GIVEN `the person is seeking to be added as a party` IS A BOOLEAN
      way IS A `o 9 r 10(2) a way a person seeking to be added may proceed`
      `the person is aware of the case conference` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the letter is addressed to the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the letter is copied to all the parties` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 10(2) the person may proceed in this way` MEANS
    IF `the person is seeking to be added as a party`
    THEN
        CONSIDER way
        WHEN `o 9 r 10(2) attend a case conference` THEN
            IF `the person is aware of the case conference`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may attend a case conference if the person is aware of it" [marginal-a]
        WHEN `o 9 r 10(2) seek a case conference by letter` THEN
            IF `the letter is addressed to the Court` AND `the letter is copied to all the parties`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by letter addressed to the Court and copied to all the parties" [marginal-b]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person seeking to be added as a party"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

-- src:848 | (3) Where a person is added as a defendant, the action is deemed to be commenced against that person on the date on which the amendment to the action is made.
@ref O 9 r 10(3) (src:848)
GIVEN `a person is added as a defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the amendment to the action is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`o 9 r 10(3) the day on which the action is deemed to be commenced against the added defendant` MEANS
    IF `a person is added as a defendant`
    THEN JUST `the date on which the amendment to the action is made`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a person is added as a defendant" (a "where" that fails, but the answer is a date, which cannot carry JUST FALSE: the yes/no twin below carries it)

-- Twin of the function above, asked as a yes/no question so that a failed "where" can answer JUST FALSE (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b)).
-- src:848 | (3) Where a person is added as a defendant, the action is deemed to be commenced against that person on the date on which the amendment to the action is made.
@ref O 9 r 10(3) (src:848)
GIVEN `a person is added as a defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the amendment to the action is made` IS A DATE
      `the day the action is said to be commenced against the person` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 10(3) the action is deemed to be commenced against the person on this day` MEANS
    IF `a person is added as a defendant`
    THEN
        IF `the day the action is said to be commenced against the person` EQUALS `the date on which the amendment to the action is made`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the action is deemed to be commenced against that person on the day on which the amendment is made" (a deeming rule that names its day)
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person is added as a defendant" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05, (b)) [marginal-a]

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 9, Rule 11 -- consolidation, etc., of causes or matters`
-- ===========================================================================

DECLARE `o 9 r 11 an order the Court may make` IS ONE OF
    `o 9 r 11 order 2 or more actions to be consolidated`
    `o 9 r 11 order them to be tried together`
    `o 9 r 11 order them to be tried one immediately after another`
    `o 9 r 11 order any of them to be stayed pending the determination of the other action or actions`

-- src:850 | 11. The Court may order 2 or more actions to be consolidated, or order them to be tried together or one immediately after another, or order any of them to be stayed pending the determination of the other action or actions, if the Court is of the opinion that — ( a )
-- src:851 | there is some common question of law in the actions;
-- src:852 | ( b )
-- src:853 | the reliefs claimed in the actions concern or arise out of the same factual situation; or
-- src:854 | ( c )
-- src:855 | it is appropriate to do so.
@ref O 9 r 11 (src:850-855)
GIVEN order IS A `o 9 r 11 an order the Court may make`
      `there are 2 or more actions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is some common question of law in the actions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reliefs claimed concern or arise out of the same factual situation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is appropriate to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 11 the Court may make this order` MEANS
    IF `there are 2 or more actions` AND (`there is some common question of law in the actions` OR `the reliefs claimed concern or arise out of the same factual situation` OR `it is appropriate to do so`)
    THEN
        CONSIDER order
        WHEN `o 9 r 11 order 2 or more actions to be consolidated` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 9 r 11 order them to be tried together` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 9 r 11 order them to be tried one immediately after another` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 9 r 11 order any of them to be stayed pending the determination of the other action or actions` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the Court is of the opinion that" (a) a common question of law, (b) the same factual situation, or (c) it is appropriate [marginal-a]

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 9, Rule 12 -- security for costs`
-- ===========================================================================

-- The three limbs of paragraph (1), each its own answer (ruling E1, option C); one function gathers them by hand (option B).
-- src:857 | 12. —(1) The defendant may apply for security for the defendant’s costs of the action if the claimant — ( a )
-- src:858 | is ordinarily resident out of the jurisdiction;
@ref O 9 r 12(1)(a) (src:857-858)
GIVEN `the claimant is ordinarily resident out of the jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 12(1)(a) the defendant may apply for security for costs because the claimant is ordinarily resident out of the jurisdiction` MEANS
    IF `the claimant is ordinarily resident out of the jurisdiction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the claimant is ordinarily resident out of the jurisdiction" [marginal-a]

-- src:859 | ( b )
-- src:860 | is a nominal claimant who is suing for some other person’s benefit (but not suing in a representative capacity) or is being funded by a non‑party, and there is reason to believe that the claimant will be unable to pay the defendant’s costs if ordered to do so; or
@ref O 9 r 12(1)(b) (src:859-860)
GIVEN `the claimant is a nominal claimant suing for some other person's benefit and not in a representative capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is being funded by a non-party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is reason to believe that the claimant will be unable to pay the defendant's costs if ordered to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 12(1)(b) the defendant may apply for security for costs because the claimant is a nominal claimant or is funded by a non-party` MEANS
    IF (`the claimant is a nominal claimant suing for some other person's benefit and not in a representative capacity` OR `the claimant is being funded by a non-party`) AND `there is reason to believe that the claimant will be unable to pay the defendant's costs if ordered to do so`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the claimant ... is a nominal claimant ... or is being funded by a non-party, and there is reason to believe that the claimant will be unable to pay" [marginal-a]

-- Fork F-O9-4: "so as to evade the consequences of the litigation" is read as qualifying all three acts of limb (c).
-- src:861 | ( c )
-- src:862 | has not stated or has incorrectly stated the claimant’s address in the originating claim or originating application, or has changed the claimant’s address during the course of the proceedings, so as to evade the consequences of the litigation.
@ref O 9 r 12(1)(c) (src:861-862)
GIVEN `the claimant has not stated or has incorrectly stated the claimant's address in the originating claim or originating application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has changed the claimant's address during the course of the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant did so to evade the consequences of the litigation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 12(1)(c) the defendant may apply for security for costs because of the claimant's address` MEANS
    IF (`the claimant has not stated or has incorrectly stated the claimant's address in the originating claim or originating application` OR `the claimant has changed the claimant's address during the course of the proceedings`) AND `the claimant did so to evade the consequences of the litigation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the claimant ... has not stated or has incorrectly stated the claimant's address ..., or has changed the claimant's address ..., so as to evade the consequences of the litigation" [marginal-a]

-- src:857 | 12. —(1) The defendant may apply for security for the defendant’s costs of the action if the claimant — ( a )
-- src:858 | is ordinarily resident out of the jurisdiction;
-- src:859 | ( b )
-- src:860 | is a nominal claimant who is suing for some other person’s benefit (but not suing in a representative capacity) or is being funded by a non‑party, and there is reason to believe that the claimant will be unable to pay the defendant’s costs if ordered to do so; or
-- src:861 | ( c )
-- src:862 | has not stated or has incorrectly stated the claimant’s address in the originating claim or originating application, or has changed the claimant’s address during the course of the proceedings, so as to evade the consequences of the litigation.
@ref O 9 r 12(1) (src:857-862)
GIVEN `limb (a) is made out` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `limb (b) is made out` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `limb (c) is made out` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 12(1) the defendant may apply for security for the defendant's costs` MEANS
    IF `limb (a) is made out` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `limb (b) is made out` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `limb (c) is made out` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        IF `limb (a) is made out` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `limb (b) is made out` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `limb (c) is made out` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The defendant may apply for security for the defendant's costs of the action if the claimant" is within (a), (b) or (c) [marginal-a]
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a limb is not covered, so the gathered answer is not covered

-- src:863 | (2) If the claimant is a company, section 388 of the Companies Act also applies.
@ref O 9 r 12(2) (src:863)
GIVEN `the claimant is a company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 12(2) section 388 of the Companies Act also applies` MEANS
    IF `the claimant is a company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the claimant is a company, section 388 of the Companies Act also applies" [marginal-a]

-- src:864 | (3) The defendant may apply for security for the defendant’s costs of the action to be provided by a non‑party, if that non‑party has — ( a )
-- src:865 | assigned that non‑party’s right in the action to the claimant in return for a share of any money or property which the claimant may recover in the action;
@ref O 9 r 12(3)(a) (src:864-865)
GIVEN `the non-party has assigned that non-party's right in the action to the claimant in return for a share of any money or property which the claimant may recover` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 12(3)(a) the defendant may apply for security for costs from the non-party who assigned a right in the action` MEANS
    IF `the non-party has assigned that non-party's right in the action to the claimant in return for a share of any money or property which the claimant may recover`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if that non-party has assigned that non-party's right in the action to the claimant in return for a share" [marginal-a]

-- src:866 | ( b )
-- src:867 | contributed or agreed to contribute to the claimant’s costs in return for a share of any money or property which the claimant may recover in the action; or
@ref O 9 r 12(3)(b) (src:866-867)
GIVEN `the non-party has contributed or agreed to contribute to the claimant's costs in return for a share of any money or property which the claimant may recover` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 12(3)(b) the defendant may apply for security for costs from the non-party who contributed in return for a share` MEANS
    IF `the non-party has contributed or agreed to contribute to the claimant's costs in return for a share of any money or property which the claimant may recover`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if that non-party has ... contributed or agreed to contribute to the claimant's costs in return for a share" [marginal-a]

-- src:868 | ( c )
-- src:869 | contributed or agreed to contribute to the claimant’s costs and actively instigates or encourages the claimant to maintain the claimant’s action.
@ref O 9 r 12(3)(c) (src:868-869)
GIVEN `the non-party has contributed or agreed to contribute to the claimant's costs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the non-party actively instigates or encourages the claimant to maintain the claimant's action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 12(3)(c) the defendant may apply for security for costs from the non-party who contributed and instigates the action` MEANS
    IF `the non-party has contributed or agreed to contribute to the claimant's costs` AND `the non-party actively instigates or encourages the claimant to maintain the claimant's action`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if that non-party has ... contributed or agreed to contribute to the claimant's costs and actively instigates or encourages the claimant" [marginal-a]

-- src:864 | (3) The defendant may apply for security for the defendant’s costs of the action to be provided by a non‑party, if that non‑party has — ( a )
-- src:865 | assigned that non‑party’s right in the action to the claimant in return for a share of any money or property which the claimant may recover in the action;
-- src:866 | ( b )
-- src:867 | contributed or agreed to contribute to the claimant’s costs in return for a share of any money or property which the claimant may recover in the action; or
-- src:868 | ( c )
-- src:869 | contributed or agreed to contribute to the claimant’s costs and actively instigates or encourages the claimant to maintain the claimant’s action.
@ref O 9 r 12(3) (src:864-869)
GIVEN `limb (a) is made out` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `limb (b) is made out` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `limb (c) is made out` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 12(3) the defendant may apply for security for the defendant's costs to be provided by a non-party` MEANS
    IF `limb (a) is made out` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `limb (b) is made out` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `limb (c) is made out` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        IF `limb (a) is made out` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `limb (b) is made out` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `limb (c) is made out` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if that non-party has" done (a), (b) or (c) [marginal-a]
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a limb is not covered, so the gathered answer is not covered

-- src:870 | (4) An application for an order under paragraph (3) must be made by summons, which must be served on the non‑party personally and on every party to the proceedings.
@ref O 9 r 12(4) (src:870)
GIVEN `the application is made by summons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the summons is served on the non-party personally` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the summons is served on every party to the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 12(4) the application for an order under paragraph (3) is made as required` MEANS
    IF `the application is made by summons` AND `the summons is served on the non-party personally` AND `the summons is served on every party to the proceedings`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be made by summons, which must be served on the non-party personally and on every party to the proceedings" (a "must" not met, fork F-must in NOTES.md) [marginal-c]

-- src:871 | (5) Nothing in this Rule is deemed to limit or affect the power of the Court to require security to be given for the costs of any proceedings under any written law.
@ref O 9 r 12(5) (src:871)
GIVEN `the power is the power of the Court under a written law to require security for the costs of proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 12(5) this Rule limits or affects the Court's power to require security under a written law` MEANS
    IF `the power is the power of the Court under a written law to require security for the costs of proceedings`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this Rule is deemed to limit or affect the power of the Court to require security to be given for the costs of any proceedings under any written law"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the denial is of an effect on the power "under any written law"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

-- src:872 | (6) The references in paragraphs (1), (2) and (3) to a claimant and a defendant are to be construed as references to the person (however described on the record) who is in the position of claimant or defendant (as the case may be) in the proceeding in question, including a proceeding on a counterclaim.
@ref O 9 r 12(6) (src:872)
GIVEN reference IS A `Role in the action`
      `the person is in that position in the proceeding in question, including a proceeding on a counterclaim, however described on the record` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 12(6) a reference in paragraphs (1), (2) and (3) is to this person` MEANS
    CONSIDER reference
    WHEN Claimant THEN
        IF `the person is in that position in the proceeding in question, including a proceeding on a counterclaim, however described on the record`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the person ... who is in the position of claimant"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))
    WHEN Defendant THEN
        IF `the person is in that position in the proceeding in question, including a proceeding on a counterclaim, however described on the record`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the person ... who is in the position of ... defendant"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))
    WHEN `Third party` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): paragraph (6) speaks of a claimant and a defendant only as the words used in paragraphs (1), (2) and (3)
    WHEN `Fourth party` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): paragraph (6) speaks of a claimant and a defendant only as the words used in paragraphs (1), (2) and (3)
    WHEN Appellant THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): paragraph (6) speaks of a claimant and a defendant only as the words used in paragraphs (1), (2) and (3)
    WHEN Respondent THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): paragraph (6) speaks of a claimant and a defendant only as the words used in paragraphs (1), (2) and (3)
    WHEN `Non-party` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): paragraph (6) speaks of a claimant and a defendant only as the words used in paragraphs (1), (2) and (3)

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 9, Rule 13 -- further and better particulars`
-- ===========================================================================

-- src:874 | 13. The Court may order a party to serve on any other party particulars of any matter stated in the firstmentioned party’s pleading if the Court is of the opinion that the particulars are necessary on the facts of the case.
@ref O 9 r 13 (src:874)
GIVEN `the Court is of the opinion that the particulars are necessary on the facts of the case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 13 the Court may order a party to serve particulars of a matter stated in the party's pleading` MEANS
    IF `the Court is of the opinion that the particulars are necessary on the facts of the case`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the Court is of the opinion that the particulars are necessary on the facts of the case" [marginal-a]

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 9, Rule 14 -- amendment of pleadings`
-- ===========================================================================

-- src:876 | 14. —(1) The Court may allow the parties to amend their pleadings. (2) In a special case, the Court may consider events that occurred after the originating claim is filed to be pleaded even though they do not relate back to the date of the filing of the originating claim.
@ref O 9 r 14(1) (src:876)
GIVEN document IS A `Document kind`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 14(1) the Court may allow the parties to amend the document` MEANS
    CONSIDER `o 1 r 3(1) a document is a pleading` document
    WHEN JUST isPleading THEN
        IF isPleading
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "their pleadings"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): whether the document is a pleading is not answered by O 1 r 3(1)

-- src:876 | 14. —(1) The Court may allow the parties to amend their pleadings. (2) In a special case, the Court may consider events that occurred after the originating claim is filed to be pleaded even though they do not relate back to the date of the filing of the originating claim.
@ref O 9 r 14(2) (src:876)
GIVEN `it is a special case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the event occurred after the originating claim is filed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 14(2) the Court may consider the event to be pleaded although it does not relate back to the date of filing` MEANS
    IF `it is a special case` AND `the event occurred after the originating claim is filed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In a special case"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

-- "less than 14 days before the commencement of the trial": the day is the 14th day before it, and the amendment
-- is barred if made after that day (a prohibition with a period: fork F-O9-3, a scope limit, ruling (c)).
-- src:877 | (3) The Court must not allow any pleading to be amended less than 14 days before the commencement of the trial except in a special case.
@ref O 9 r 14(3) (src:877)
GIVEN `the date of the amendment` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the day 14 days before the commencement of the trial` IS A DATE
      `it is a special case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 14(3) the Court may allow the pleading to be amended` MEANS
    IF `the date of the amendment` GREATER THAN `o 3 r 3 the day 14 days before the commencement of the trial` AND (NOT `it is a special case`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Court must not allow any pleading to be amended less than 14 days before the commencement of the trial except in a special case" (flat negative, ruling N2)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is for an amendment "less than 14 days before the commencement of the trial" and not in a special case; outside it paragraph (3) is silent [marginal-b]

DECLARE `o 9 r 14(4) a circumstance after the limitation period has expired` IS ONE OF
    `o 9 r 14(4)(a) an amendment to correct the name of a party`
    `o 9 r 14(4)(b) an amendment to alter the capacity in which a party sues`
    `o 9 r 14(4)(c) an amendment to add or substitute a new cause of action`
    `o 9 r 14(4) any other amendment`

-- src:878 | (4) Where an application for permission to amend is made after the relevant limitation period has expired, the Court may allow the amendment in the following circumstances: ( a )
-- src:879 | an amendment to correct the name of a party even if its alleged effect will be to substitute a new party, if it was a genuine mistake and was not misleading as to the identity of the party in question;
-- src:880 | ( b )
-- src:881 | an amendment to alter the capacity in which a party sues, if the party might have sued in that capacity at the time the originating claim was issued or the counterclaim was made;
-- src:882 | ( c )
-- src:883 | an amendment to add or substitute a new cause of action, if the new cause of action arises out of the same or substantially the same facts as an existing cause of action for which relief has already been claimed in the same action.
@ref O 9 r 14(4) (src:878-883)
GIVEN `the relevant limitation period has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
      circumstance IS A `o 9 r 14(4) a circumstance after the limitation period has expired`
      `it was a genuine mistake and was not misleading as to the identity of the party in question` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party might have sued in that capacity at the time the originating claim was issued or the counterclaim was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the new cause of action arises out of the same or substantially the same facts as an existing cause of action for which relief has already been claimed in the same action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 14(4) the Court may allow the amendment` MEANS
    IF `the relevant limitation period has expired`
    THEN
        CONSIDER circumstance
        WHEN `o 9 r 14(4)(a) an amendment to correct the name of a party` THEN
            IF `it was a genuine mistake and was not misleading as to the identity of the party in question`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it was a genuine mistake and was not misleading as to the identity of the party in question" [marginal-a]
        WHEN `o 9 r 14(4)(b) an amendment to alter the capacity in which a party sues` THEN
            IF `the party might have sued in that capacity at the time the originating claim was issued or the counterclaim was made`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the party might have sued in that capacity at the time the originating claim was issued or the counterclaim was made" [marginal-a]
        WHEN `o 9 r 14(4)(c) an amendment to add or substitute a new cause of action` THEN
            IF `the new cause of action arises out of the same or substantially the same facts as an existing cause of action for which relief has already been claimed in the same action`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the new cause of action arises out of the same or substantially the same facts as an existing cause of action for which relief has already been claimed in the same action" [marginal-a]
        WHEN `o 9 r 14(4) any other amendment` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "the Court may allow the amendment in the following circumstances" does not say that no other circumstance will do
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an application for permission to amend is made after the relevant limitation period has expired" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))

