      ground IS A `o 9 r 17(1) the ground for summary judgment`
      `the defendant has no defence on that ground` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 17(1) the claimant may apply for summary judgment against the defendant` MEANS
    IF `the action is commenced by originating claim` AND `the defence has been filed and served` AND `the defendant has no defence on that ground`
    THEN
        CONSIDER ground
        WHEN `o 9 r 17(1)(a) the defendant has no defence to a claim` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 9 r 17(1)(b) the defendant has no defence to a particular part of a claim` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 9 r 17(1)(c) the defendant has no defence to a claim or part of a claim, except as to the amount of any damages claimed` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "after the defence has been filed and served in an originating claim on the ground that the defendant has no defence" [marginal-a]

