    IF `the action is commenced by originating claim` AND `the defendant has served a counterclaim on the claimant` AND `the claimant has served a defence to the counterclaim` AND `the claimant has no defence to a claim made in the counterclaim or to a particular part of it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a defendant to an action commenced by originating claim has served a counterclaim on the claimant and the claimant has served a defence to the counterclaim" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))

-- src:929 | (12) In relation to an application under paragraph (11), the rules in paragraphs (2) to (10) apply as they apply in relation to an application under paragraph (1), with the necessary modifications.
@ref O 9 r 17(12) (src:929)
GIVEN `the application is under paragraph (11)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 17(12) a paragraph applies to the application under paragraph (11) with the necessary modifications` MEANS
    IF `the application is under paragraph (11)` AND `paragraph number` AT LEAST 2 AND `paragraph number` AT MOST 10
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the rules in paragraphs (2) to (10)"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

-- src:930 | (13) Except where the Court otherwise permits, an application under this Rule may not be made after the expiry of 28 days after the date of service of the defence or defence to counterclaim, as the case may be.
@ref O 9 r 17(13) (src:930)
GIVEN `the date of the application` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
      `the Court otherwise permits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 17(13) the application is made in time` MEANS
    IF `the date of the application` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        IF `the Court otherwise permits`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an application under this Rule may not be made after the expiry of 28 days after the date of service of the defence or defence to counterclaim" (flat negative, and a period the text fixes in its own words, rulings N2 and 2026-11-05 (a))

-- src:930 | (13) Except where the Court otherwise permits, an application under this Rule may not be made after the expiry of 28 days after the date of service of the defence or defence to counterclaim, as the case may be.
@ref O 9 r 17(13) (src:930)
`o 9 r 17(13) twenty-eight days after the date of service of the defence` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 28
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 9, Rule 18 -- agreement on facts and law`
-- ===========================================================================

DECLARE `o 9 r 18(1) a direction the Court must give` IS ONE OF
    `o 9 r 18(1) direct the parties to agree on as many material facts as possible`
    `o 9 r 18(1) direct the parties to set them out in an agreed statement of facts at as early a stage as possible`

-- src:932 | 18. —(1) The Court must direct the parties to agree on as many material facts as possible and to set them out in an agreed statement of facts at as early a stage as possible. (2) Where admissions of fact are made by a party in the party’s pleadings or other documents, the Court may, on application made orally or in writing, give judgment on those admissions.
@ref O 9 r 18(1) (src:932)
GIVEN direction IS A `o 9 r 18(1) a direction the Court must give`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 18(1) the Court must give this direction` MEANS
    CONSIDER direction
    WHEN `o 9 r 18(1) direct the parties to agree on as many material facts as possible` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 9 r 18(1) direct the parties to set them out in an agreed statement of facts at as early a stage as possible` THEN JUST TRUE

-- src:932 | 18. —(1) The Court must direct the parties to agree on as many material facts as possible and to set them out in an agreed statement of facts at as early a stage as possible. (2) Where admissions of fact are made by a party in the party’s pleadings or other documents, the Court may, on application made orally or in writing, give judgment on those admissions.
@ref O 9 r 18(2) (src:932)
GIVEN `admissions of fact are made by a party in the party's pleadings or other documents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a party applies orally or in writing for judgment on the admissions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 18(2) the Court may give judgment on the admissions` MEANS
    IF `admissions of fact are made by a party in the party's pleadings or other documents`
    THEN
        IF `a party applies orally or in writing for judgment on the admissions`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on application made orally or in writing" [marginal-b]
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where admissions of fact are made by a party in the party's pleadings or other documents" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))

DECLARE `o 9 r 18(3) a thing the parties may do` IS ONE OF
    `o 9 r 18(3) agree on material questions of law`
    `o 9 r 18(3) waive their right of appeal`
    `o 9 r 18(3) limit their right of appeal`

-- src:933 | (3) The parties may also agree on material questions of law and to waive or limit their right of appeal.
@ref O 9 r 18(3) (src:933)
GIVEN thing IS A `o 9 r 18(3) a thing the parties may do`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 18(3) the parties may do this` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `o 9 r 18(3) agree on material questions of law` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 9 r 18(3) waive their right of appeal` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 9 r 18(3) limit their right of appeal` THEN JUST TRUE

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 9, Rule 19 -- decision on questions of law or construction of documents`
-- ===========================================================================

-- src:935 | 19. —(1) Upon a party’s application or on the Court’s own accord, the Court may decide any question of law or the construction of any document arising in any action without a trial or hearing on the facts, whether or not such decision will fully determine the action. (2) Where the Court’s decision in paragraph (1) fully determines (subject only to any appeal) the entire matter or any claim or issue therein, the Court may give judgment or dismiss the action or make any order that is appropriate.
@ref O 9 r 19(1) (src:935)
GIVEN `a question of law or the construction of a document arises in the action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a party applies or the Court acts on its own accord` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 19(1) the Court may decide the question of law or the construction of the document without a trial or hearing on the facts` MEANS
    IF `a question of law or the construction of a document arises in the action`
    THEN
        IF `a party applies or the Court acts on its own accord`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Upon a party's application or on the Court's own accord" (an "upon" read as "where", ruling of 2026-11-05) [marginal-a]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any question of law or the construction of any document arising in any action"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

-- src:935 | 19. —(1) Upon a party’s application or on the Court’s own accord, the Court may decide any question of law or the construction of any document arising in any action without a trial or hearing on the facts, whether or not such decision will fully determine the action. (2) Where the Court’s decision in paragraph (1) fully determines (subject only to any appeal) the entire matter or any claim or issue therein, the Court may give judgment or dismiss the action or make any order that is appropriate.
@ref O 9 r 19(2) (src:935)
GIVEN `the Court's decision fully determines (subject only to any appeal) the entire matter or any claim or issue in it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 19(2) the Court may give judgment or dismiss the action or make any order that is appropriate` MEANS
    IF `the Court's decision fully determines (subject only to any appeal) the entire matter or any claim or issue in it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the Court's decision in paragraph (1) fully determines (subject only to any appeal) the entire matter or any claim or issue therein" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
